 2. 🚁 Uber wants 1 million drone deliveries a day 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Image: Uber Uber is investing in drone delivery company Zipline and aiming for 1 million daily Uber Eats drone deliveries by the end of 2029, Axios' Joann Muller reports. 

 Zipline drone delivery via Uber Eats will begin in Houston and Dallas before the end of the year, then expand into dozens of other U.S. cities. 🚛 The big picture: The deal is part of Uber's effort to build a flexible delivery network of couriers, sidewalk robots and drones.

 Zipline, a San Francisco-based drone company, got its start delivering medical supplies by drone in Rwanda. It now serves medical facilities, retailers and small businesses. Go deeper ... Read the announcement . 

 
 
